$DIR/test.p:88:8: union U has no variants
    A union value holds one of its variants, so a union needs at least one.
    Variants are written like struct fields: a name, and a payload type if the
    variant carries data.
    (see "Unions" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2403" for a longer explanation)
